This error (`ERROR: 42P07: relation "users" already exists`) is actually **good news**! It means your database tables are already set up correctly from a previous attempt. You generally **do not need to do anything** if you see this—you can just proceed to use your app.

However, if you want to **wipe everything clean** and start fresh (delete all existing test data/users), you should run a "Reset" script that deletes the old tables before creating new ones.

**What to do:**
1.  Go back to the **Supabase SQL Editor**.
2.  Delete the code currently in the window.
3.  Paste and Run this **Reset Script** below:

```sql
-- 1. DROP OLD TABLES (Clear Data)
drop table if exists votes;
drop table if exists audit_logs;
drop table if exists users;
drop table if exists candidates;
drop table if exists settings;
drop table if exists positions;
drop table if exists departments;

-- 2. RE-CREATE TABLES
create extension if not exists "uuid-ossp";

create table public.users (
  id uuid default uuid_generate_v4() primary key,
  full_name text not null,
  matric_no text unique not null,
  department text not null,
  role text not null default 'student',
  status text not null default 'pending',
  password_hash text not null,
  id_card_url text,
  rejection_reason text,
  created_at bigint not null,
  email text
);

create table public.votes (
  id uuid default uuid_generate_v4() primary key,
  student_id text not null,
  candidate_id text not null,
  position text not null,
  timestamp bigint not null
);

create table public.audit_logs (
  id uuid default uuid_generate_v4() primary key,
  actor_id text,
  actor_role text,
  action_type text,
  details text,
  target_id text,
  timestamp bigint not null
);

create table public.candidates (
  id uuid default uuid_generate_v4() primary key,
  name text not null,
  matric_no text,
  department text,
  position text,
  manifesto text,
  photo_url text
);

create table public.settings (
  id int primary key default 1,
  start_date text,
  end_date text,
  is_voting_enabled boolean
);
insert into public.settings (id, start_date, end_date, is_voting_enabled)
values (1, '2024-01-01', '2024-12-31', true) on conflict do nothing;

create table public.positions (name text primary key);
insert into public.positions (name) values 
('President'), ('Vice President'), ('General Secretary'), ('Financial Secretary'), ('P.R.O');

create table public.departments (name text primary key);
insert into public.departments (name) values 
('Computer Science'), ('Software Engineering'), ('Cyber Security');

-- Enable Realtime
alter publication supabase_realtime add table public.votes;
alter publication supabase_realtime add table public.users;
```

I have also updated your app code below to auto-correct any typos (like extra spaces) in your Vercel API Keys, which is the most common cause of "Failed to fetch" errors.

The "Invalid Credentials" error is happening because the logic I added previously had a safety check (`existingAdmins.length === 0`) that might be preventing the Admin account from being created if *any* other admin (or a ghost record) exists.

I will simplify the logic: **If the user 'admin' does not exist, create it immediately.**

I have also added better error logging to the browser console (F12) so you can see exactly why it fails if it happens again.

### **Steps to Fix:**
1.  **Redeploy** this code to Vercel.
2.  Open the **Login Page**.
3.  Open your browser console (**F12** > **Console** tab) to see debug logs if needed.
4.  Login with **Matric No:** `admin` and **Password:** `admin123`.
5.  It should now auto-create the account and log you in.

# Updated files:

## services/mockDb.ts

Simplified the Admin Auto-Seeding logic to force creation if the 'admin' account is missing, removing unnecessary checks that could block it. Added detailed error logging.

```typescript
